    "intro_html":  "\u003cp\u003eFilipino adobo is soy, vinegar, garlic, and bay simmered into something far bigger than its four main parts. We built it into a burrito that holds the line at {{cal}} calories with {{protein}} grams of protein, on a tortilla carrying 18 grams of fiber for about 5 grams of net carb. If you already love our Slow Cooker Chicken Adobo Rice Bowls, think of this as the handheld cousin: pan-seared instead of braised, wrapped around rice and black beans with a bright tomato and red onion salsa to cut the salt.\u003c/p\u003e",
